    narr:narration """On 2026-07-20, Quinton Fairweather announces the organization is [adopting Zypherion for the analytics pipeline](narr:Expr_1LifecycleStepA_1), grounding the decision in a [performance claim of 15x faster columnar queries](narr:Expr_1LifecycleStepA_2) and committing to a [migration start next quarter](narr:Expr_1LifecycleStepA_3). These three utterances form a single continuous quoted speech act — adoption, justification, timeline — delivered in calm, technical register with legitimate authority. A composer-editorial layer by XenaExpertgh then [restates the database choice](narr:Expr_1LifecycleStepA_5), [restates the performance figure](narr:Expr_1LifecycleStepA_6), and [pins the timeline to Q3 2026](narr:Expr_1LifecycleStepA_7) in parallel bullet form, converting the spoken declaration into a matter-of-fact summary. The hub thus holds both the raw declarative moment and its editorial compression side by side. The 15x improvement figure is the sole quantitative warrant for the migration and rests entirely on Quinton's expert assertion — no independent benchmark or dissenting voice appears within this graph.""" ;
